# Change Management

- Keep changes scoped and reviewable.
- Use branches/worktrees for concurrent agent work where appropriate.
- Do not mix unrelated refactors into security-critical changes.
- When an accepted architectural invariant changes, update the decision log and corresponding rule.
- Prefer backward-compatible migrations and explicit rollback paths for persistent state.
- Treat generated artifacts and vendored upstream code carefully; do not rewrite upstream sources without a documented reason.
